a interfaz de usuario de una aplicación web","fr":"Les tests frontend sont des tests qui vérifient la fonctionnalité de l''interface utilisateur d''une application web","de":"Frontend-Tests sind Tests, die die Funktionalität der Benutzeroberfläche einer Webanwendung überprüfen","pt":"O que é teste frontend? É uma habilidade que gera testes de alta qualidade para componentes e utilitários","ru":"Что такое фронтенд-тестирование? Это навык, который генерирует высококачественные тесты для компонентов и утилит","ar":"ما هو اختبار الواجهة الأمامية? هو مهارة تنتج اختبارات عالية الجودة للمكونات والبرامج المساعدة"},"features":{"en":["Generates high-quality frontend tests using Vitest mock/timer APIs","Supports writing tests for components, hooks, and utilities","Enables review of existing tests for completeness","Applies established conventions and best practices for frontend testing","Utilizes vi.* APIs for efficient testing"],"zh":["生成高质量的自动化测试","支持Vitest mock/timer APIs","提高代码可靠性和稳定性","适用于组件、钩子和实用程序的测试","支持测试代码的审查和完善"],"ja":["高品質の自動テストを生成","Vitest mock/timer APIsをサポート","コードの信頼性と安定性を向上","コンポーネント、フック、ユーティリティのテストに適しています","テストコードのレビューと完善をサポート"],"ko":["고품질의 자동화 테스트를 생성","Vitest mock/timer APIs를 지원","코드의 신뢰성과 안정성을 향상","컴포넌트, 훅, 유틸리티의 테스트에 적합","테스트 코드의 리뷰와 완善을 지원"],"es":["Generación de pruebas frontend con Vitest","Uso de APIs de mock y temporizador de Vitest (vi.*)","Seguimiento de convenciones y mejores prácticas establecidas","Compatibilidad con componentes, hooks y utilidades","Revisión de pruebas existentes para completitud"],"fr":["Génération de tests frontend avec Vitest","Utilisation des APIs de mock et de temporisation de Vitest (vi.*)","Suivi des conventions et des meilleures pratiques établies","Compatibilité avec les composants, les hooks et les utilités","Révision des tests existants pour la complétude"],"de":["Erstellung von Frontend-Tests mit Vitest","Verwendung von Vitest-Mock- und Timer-APIs (vi.*)","Einhaltung etablierter Konventionen und Best Practices","Kompatibilität mit Komponenten, Hooks und Utilities","Überprüfung von bestehenden Tests auf Vollständigkeit"],"pt":["Geração de testes com Vitest","Uso de APIs de mock e temporizador do Vitest","Suporte a testes de componentes e utilitários","Seguimento de convenções estabelecidas","Integração com o projeto Dify"],"ru":["Генерация тестов с Vitest","Использование API-мок и таймера Vitest","Поддержка тестирования компонентов и утилит","Следование установленным конвенциям","Интеграция с проектом Dify и ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["توليد اختبارات مع Vitest","استخدام واجهات برمجة التطبيقات لمواكب وتايمر Vitest","دعم اختبار المكونات والبرامج المساعدة","التعاون مع الاتفاقيات المعمول بها","التكامل مع مشروع Dify ووكيلات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use frontend-testing","what is frontend-testing","frontend-testing alternative","frontend-testing vs Jest","frontend-testing install","frontend-testing setup guide","Vitest mock/timer APIs tutorial","comprehensive frontend test generation"],"zh":["前端测试","自动化测试","Vitest","mock/timer APIs","代码可靠性","代码稳定性","AIエージェント","前端开发"],"ja":["フロントエンドテスト","自動テスト","Vitest","mock/timer APIs","コードの信頼性","コードの安定性","AIエージェント","フロントエンド開発"],"ko":["프런트엔드 테스트","자동화 테스트","Vitest","mock/timer APIs","코드의 신뢰성","코드의 안정성","AI 에이전트","프런트엔드 개발"],"es":["pruebas frontend","Vitest","tests automatizados","desarrollo web","Dify","mejores prácticas de pruebas","convenciones de pruebas","generación de pruebas","revisión de pruebas"],"fr":["tests frontend","Vitest","tests automatisés","développement web","Dify","meilleures pratiques de tests","conventions de tests","génération de tests","révision de tests"],"de":["Frontend-Tests","Vitest","automatisierte Tests","Webentwicklung","Dify","Best Practices für Tests","Testkonventionen","Testgenerierung","Testüberprüfung"],"pt":["teste frontend","Vitest","testes de componente","testes de utilitário","convenções de teste","projeto Dify","desenvolvimento frontend","ferramentas de teste","melhores práticas de teste"],"ru":["фронтенд-тестирование","Vitest","тестирование компонентов","тестирование утилит","конвенции тестирования","проект Dify","разработка фронтенда","инструменты тестирования","лучшие практики тестирования","ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["اختبار الواجهة الأمامية","Vitest","اختبار المكونات","اختبار البرامج المساعدة","اتفاقيات الاختبار","مشروع Dify","تطوير الواجهة الأمامية","أدوات الاختبار","أفضل الممارسات للاختبار","وكيلات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"allthingslinux","repo":"portal","repoPath":"allthingslinux/portal","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.472Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-testing","description":"Generate Vitest + React Testing Library tests for Dify frontend components, hooks, and utilities. Triggers on testing, spec files, coverage, Vitest, RTL, unit tests, integration tests, or write/review test requests.","bodyPreview":"# Dify Frontend Testing Skill\n\nThis skill enables Claude to generate high-quality, comprehensive frontend tests for the Dify project following established conventions and best practices.\n\n> **⚠️ Authoritative Source**: This skill is derived from `web/testing/testing.md`. Use Vitest mock/timer APIs (`vi.*`).\n\n## When to Apply This Skill\n\nApply this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks to **write tests** for a component, hook, or utility\n- Asks to **review existing tests** for completeness\n- Mentions **Vi","body":"# Dify Frontend Testing Skill\n\nThis skill enables Claude to generate high-quality, comprehensive frontend tests for the Dify project following established conventions and best practices.\n\n> **⚠️ Authoritative Source**: This skill is derived from `web/testing/testing.md`. Use Vitest mock/timer APIs (`vi.*`).\n\n## When to Apply This Skill\n\nApply this skill when the user:\n\n- Asks to **write tests** for a component, hook, or utility\n- Asks to **review existing tests** for completeness\n- Mentions **Vitest**, **React Testing Library**, **RTL**, or **spec files**\n- Requests **test coverage** improvement\n- Uses `pnpm analyze-component` output as context\n- Mentions **testing**, **unit tests**, or **integration tests** for frontend code\n- Wants to understand **testing patterns** in the Dify codebase\n\n**Do NOT apply** when:\n\n- User is asking about backend/API tests (Python/pytest)\n- User is asking about E2E tests (Playwright/Cypress)\n- User is only asking conceptual questions without code context\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Tech Stack\n\n| Tool | Version | Purpose |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| Vitest | 4.0.16 | Test runner |\n| React Testing Library | 16.0 | Component testing |\n| jsdom | - | Test environment |\n| nock | 14.0 | HTTP mocking |\n| TypeScript | 5.x | Type safety |\n\n### Key Commands\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\npnpm test\n\n# Watch mode\npnpm test:watch\n\n# Run specific file\npnpm test path/to/file.spec.tsx\n\n# Generate coverage report\npnpm test:coverage\n\n# Analyze component complexity\npnpm analyze-component <path>\n\n# Review existing test\npnpm analyze-component <path> --review\n```\n\n### File Naming\n\n- Test files: `ComponentName.spec.tsx` (same directory as component)\n- Integration tests: `web/__tests__/` directory\n\n## Test Structure Template\n\n```typescript\nimport { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor } from ''@testing-library/react''\nimport Component from ''./index''\n\n// ✅ Import real project components (DO NOT mock these)\n// import Loading from ''@/app/components/base/loading''\n// import { ChildComponent } from ''./child-component''\n\n// ✅ Mock external dependencies only\nvi.mock(''@/service/api'')\nvi.mock(''next/navigation'', () => ({\n  useRouter: () => ({ push: vi.fn() }),\n  usePathname: () => ''/test'',\n}))\n\n// ✅ Zustand stores: Use real stores (auto-mocked globally)\n// Set test state with: useAppStore.setState({ ... })\n\n// Shared state for mocks (if needed)\nlet mockSharedState = false\n\ndescribe(''ComponentName'', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    vi.clearAllMocks()  // ✅ Reset mocks BEFORE each test\n    mockSharedState = false  // ✅ Reset shared state\n  })\n\n  // Rendering tests (REQUIRED)\n  describe(''Rendering'', () => {\n    it(''should render without crashing'', () => {\n      // Arrange\n      const props = { title: ''Test'' }\n      \n      // Act\n      render(<Component {...props} />)\n      \n      // Assert\n      expect(screen.getByText(''Test'')).toBeInTheDocument()\n    })\n  })\n\n  // Props tests (REQUIRED)\n  describe(''Props'', () => {\n    it(''should apply custom className'', () => {\n      render(<Component className=\"custom\" />)\n      expect(screen.getByRole(''button'')).toHaveClass(''custom'')\n    })\n  })\n\n  // User Interactions\n  describe(''User Interactions'', () => {\n    it(''should handle click events'', () => {\n      const handleClick = vi.fn()\n      render(<Component onClick={handleClick} />)\n      \n      fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole(''button''))\n      \n      expect(handleClick).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)\n    })\n  })\n\n  // Edge Cases (REQUIRED)\n  describe(''Edge Cases'', () => {\n    it(''should handle null data'', () => {\n      render(<Component data={null} />)\n      expect(screen.getByText(/no data/i)).toBeInTheDocument()\n    })\n\n    it(''should handle empty array'', () => {\n      render(<Component items={[]} />)\n      expect(screen.getByText(/empty/i)).toBeInTheDocument()\n    })\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Testing Workflow (CRITICAL)\n\n### ⚠️ Incremental Approach Required\n\n**NEVER generate all test files at once.** For complex components or multi-file directories:\n\n1. **Analyze & Plan**: List all files, order by complexity (simple → complex)\n1. **Process ONE at a time**: Write test → Run test → Fix if needed → Next\n1. **Verify before proceeding**: Do NOT continue to next file until current passes\n\n```\nFor each file:\n  ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ 1. Write test                          │\n  │ 2. Run: pnpm test <file>.spec.tsx      │\n  │ 3. PASS? → Mark complete, next file    │\n  │    FAIL? → Fix first, then continue    │\n  └────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Complexity-Based Order\n\nProcess in this order for multi-file testing:\n\n1. 🟢 Utility functions (simplest)\n1. 🟢 Custom hooks\n1. 🟡 Simple components (presentational)\n1. 🟡 Medium components (state, effects)\n1. 🔴 Complex components (API, routing)\n1. 🔴 Integration tests (index files - last)\n\n### When to Refactor First\n\n- **Complexity > 50**: Break into smaller pieces before testing\n- **500+ lines**: Consider splitting before testing\n- **Many dependencies**: Extract logic into hooks first\n\n> 📖 See `references/workflow.md` for complete workflow details and todo list format.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Path-Level Testing (Directory Testing)\n\nWhen assigned to test a directory/path, test **ALL content** within that path:\n\n- Test all components, hooks, utilities in the directory (not just `index` file)\n- Use incremental approach: one file at a time, verify each before proceeding\n- Goal: 100% coverage of ALL files in the directory\n\n### Integration Testing First\n\n**Prefer integration testing** when writing tests for a directory:\n\n- ✅ **Import real project components** directly (including base components and siblings)\n- ✅ **Only mock**: API services (`@/service/*`), `next/navigation`, complex context providers\n- ❌ **DO NOT mock** base components (`@/app/components/base/*`)\n- ❌ **DO NOT mock** sibling/child components in the same directory\n\n> See [Test Structure Template](#test-structure-template) for correct import/mock patterns.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. AAA Pattern (Arrange-Act-Assert)\n\nEvery test should clearly separate:\n\n- **Arrange**: Setup test data and render component\n- **Act**: Perform user actions\n- **Assert**: Verify expected outcomes\n\n### 2. Black-Box Testing\n\n- Test observable behavior, not implementation details\n- Use semantic queries (getByRole, getByLabelText)\n- Avoid testing internal state directly\n- **Prefer pattern matching over hardcoded strings** in assertions:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Avoid: hardcoded text assertions\nexpect(screen.getByText(''Loading...'')).toBeInTheDocument()\n\n// ✅ Better: role-based queries\nexpect(screen.getByRole(''status'')).toBeInTheDocument()\n\n// ✅ Better: pattern matching\nexpect(screen.getByText(/loading/i)).toBeInTheDocument()\n```\n\n### 3. Single Behavior Per Test\n\nEach test verifies ONE user-observable behavior:\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ Good: One behavior\nit(''should disable button when loading'', () => {\n  render(<Button loading />)\n  expect(screen.getByRole(''button'')).toBeDisabled()\n})\n\n// ❌ Bad: Multiple behaviors\nit(''should handle loading state'', () => {\n  render(<Button loading />)\n  expect(screen.getByRole(''button'')).toBeDisabled()\n  expect(screen.getByText(''Loading...'')).toBeInTheDocument()\n  expect(screen.getByRole(''button'')).toHaveClass(''loading'')\n})\n```\n\n### 4. Semantic Naming\n\nUse `should <behavior> when <condition>`:\n\n```typescript\nit(''should show error message when validation fails'')\nit(''should call onSubmit when form is valid'')\nit(''should disable input when isReadOnly is true'')\n```\n\n## Required Test Scenarios\n\n### Always Required (All Components)\n\n1. **Rendering**: Component renders without crashing\n1. **Props**: Required props, optional props, default values\n1. **Edge Cases**: null, undefined, empty values, boundary conditions\n\n### Conditional (When Present)\n\n| Feature | Test Focus |\n|---------|-----------|\n| `useState` | Initial state, transitions, cleanup |\n| `useEffect` | Execution, dependencies, cleanup |\n| Event handlers | All onClick, onChange, onSubmit, keyboard |\n| API calls | Loading, success, error states |\n| Routing | Navigation, params, query strings |\n| `useCallback`/`useMemo` | Referential equality |\n| Context | Provider values, consumer behavior |\n| Forms | Validation, submission, error display |\n\n## Coverage Goals (Per File)\n\nFor each test file generated, aim for:\n\n- ✅ **100%** function coverage\n- ✅ **100%** statement coverage\n- ✅ **>95%** branch coverage\n- ✅ **>95%** line coverage\n\n> **Note**: For multi-file directories, process one file at a time with full coverage each. See `references/workflow.md`.\n\n## Detailed Guides\n\nFor more detailed information, refer to:\n\n- `references/workflow.md` - **Incremental testing workflow** (MUST READ for multi-file testing)\n- `references/mocking.md` - Mock patterns, Zustand store testing, and best practices\n- `references/async-testing.md` - Async operations and API calls\n- `references/domain-components.md` - Workflow, Dataset, Configuration testing\n- `references/common-patterns.md` - Frequently used testing patterns\n- `references/checklist.md` - Test generation checklist and validation steps\n\n## Authoritative References\n\n### Primary Specification (MUST follow)\n\n- **`web/testing/testing.md`** - The canonical testing specification. This skill is derived from this document.\n\n### Reference Examples in Codebase\n\n- `web/utils/classnames.spec.ts` - Utility function tests\n- `web/app/components/base/button/index.spec.tsx` - Component tests\n- `web/__mocks__/provider-context.ts` - Mock factory example\n\n### Project Configuration\n\n- `web/vitest.config.ts` - Vitest configuration\n- `web/vitest.setup.ts` - Test environment setup\n- `web/scripts/analyze-component.js` - Component analysis tool\n- Modules are not mocked automatically. Global mocks live in `web/vitest.setup.ts` (for example `react-i18next`, `next/image`); mock other modules like `ky` or `mime` locally in test files.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:09:35.832Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for JavaScript-focused AI Agents like Claude, needing comprehensive frontend testing capabilities with Vitest","zh":"适合于像 Claude 这样的面向 JavaScript 的 AI Agent，需要使用 Vitest 进行全面前端测试的能力","ja":"Claude のような JavaScript フォーカスの AI エージェントに適しています。Vitest を使用した包括的なフロントエンド テスト機能が必要です","ko":"Claude 같은 JavaScript 중점의 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. Vitest를 사용한 포괄적인 프론트엔드 테스트 기능이 필요한 경우","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial centrados en JavaScript como Claude, que necesitan capacidades de prueba de frontend integrales con Vitest","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur JavaScript comme Claude, nécessitant des capacités de test de frontend complètes avec Vitest","de":"Ideal für JavaScript-fokussierte KI-Agenten wie Claude, die umfassende Frontend-Testfunktionen mit Vitest benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA focados em JavaScript, como Claude, que necessitam de capacidades de teste de frontend abrangentes com Vitest","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на JavaScript, таких как Claude, требующих всесторонних возможностей тестирования frontend с Vitest","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذكية التي تركز على جافا سكريبت مثل Claude، وتحتاج إلى قدرات اختبار واجهة المستخدم الشاملة مع Vitest"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate high-quality, comprehensive frontend tests following established conventions and best practices, utilizing Vitest mock/timer APIs, and benefiting developers working on projects like Dify","zh":"赋予代理生成高质量、全面的前端测试的能力，遵循既定的惯例和最佳实践，利用 Vitest mock/timer APIs，并有利于开发人员在 Dify 等项目上工作","ja":"エージェントが高品質で包括的なフロントエンド テストを生成する能力を付与します。既定の規約とベスト プラクティスに従い、Vitest mock/timer APIs を利用し、Dify などのプロジェクトで作業する開発者に利益をもたらします","ko":"에이전트가 높은 품질의 포괄적인 프론트엔드 테스트를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 확립된 규약 및 모범 사례를 따르며 Vitest mock/timer API를 사용하며 Dify 같은 프로젝트에서 일하는 개발자에게 도움이 됩니다","es":"Permite a los agentes generar pruebas de frontend de alta calidad y completas siguiendo convenciones y mejores prácticas establecidas, utilizando las APIs de Vitest mock/timer y beneficiando a los desarrolladores que trabajan en proyectos como Dify","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des tests de frontend de haute qualité et complets en suivant des conventions et des meilleures pratiques établies, en utilisant les API Vitest mock/timer et en bénéficiant aux développeurs qui travaillent sur des projets comme Dify","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, hochwertige und umfassende Frontend-Tests nach etablierten Konventionen und Best Practices zu generieren, indem Vitest mock/timer APIs verwendet werden und Entwicklern an Projekten wie Dify zugutekommt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar testes de frontend de alta qualidade e abrangentes, seguindo convenções e práticas recomendadas estabelecidas, utilizando APIs de mock/timer do Vitest e beneficiando os desenvolvedores que trabalham em projetos como Dify","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать высококачественные и всесторонние тесты frontend, следующие установленным конвенциям и лучшим практикам, используя API mock/timer Vitest и принося пользу разработчикам, работающим над проектами, такими как Dify","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من توليد اختبارات واجهة المستخدم عالية الجودة وشاملة، متبعة الاتفاقيات وأفضل الممارسات المعمول بها، وتستخدم API mock/timer من Vitest وتفيد المطورين العاملين على مشاريع مثل Dify"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating tests for components, hooks, or utilities","Reviewing existing tests for completeness","Creating tests using Vitest mock/timer APIs"],"zh":["为组件、钩子或实用程序生成测试","查看现有测试的完整性","使用 Vitest mock/timer APIs 创建测试"],"ja":["コンポーネント、フック、またはユーティリティのテストを生成する","既存のテストの完全性を確認する","Vitest mock/timer APIs を使用してテストを作成する"],"ko":["컴포넌트, 훅 또는 유틸리티에 대한 테스트 생성","기존 테스트의 완전성 검토","Vitest mock/timer API를 사용하여 테스트 생성"],"es":["Generar pruebas para componentes, ganchos o utilidades","Revisar pruebas existentes para garantizar la completitud","Crear pruebas utilizando las APIs de Vitest mock/timer"],"fr":["Générer des tests pour les composants, les crochets ou les utilitaires","Réviser les tests existants pour garantir l''exhaustivité","Créer des tests en utilisant les API Vitest mock/timer"],"de":["Generieren von Tests für Komponenten, Hooks oder Utilitys","Überprüfen bestehender Tests auf Vollständigkeit","Erstellen von Tests unter Verwendung von Vitest mock/timer APIs"],"pt":["Gerar testes para componentes, hooks ou utilitários","Revisar testes existentes para completude","Criar testes usando APIs de mock/timer do Vitest"],"ru":["Генерировать тесты для компонентов, хуков или утилит","Проверять существующие тесты на полноту","Создавать тесты с использованием API mock/timer Vitest"],"ar":["توليد اختبارات للمكونات أو Hooks أو أدوات","استعراض الاختبارات الحالية للكامل","إنشاء اختبارات باستخدام API mock/timer من Vitest"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Vitest environment","Derived from web/testing/testing.md","Specific to frontend testing with Vitest"],"zh":["需要 Vitest 环境","源自 web/testing/testing.md","特定于使用 Vitest 的前端测试"],"ja":["Vitest 環境が必要","web/testing/testing.md から派生","Vitest を使用したフロントエンド テストに特定"],"ko":["Vitest 환경이 필요","web/testing/testing.md에서 파생","Vitest를 사용한 프론트엔드 테스트에 특정"],"es":["Requiere un entorno Vitest","Derivado de web/testing/testing.md","Específico para pruebas de frontend con Vitest"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Vitest","Dérivé de web/testing/testing.md","Spécifique aux tests de frontend avec Vitest"],"de":["Benötigt eine Vitest-Umgebung","Abgeleitet von web/testing/testing.md","Spezifisch für Frontend-Tests mit Vitest"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Vitest","Derivado de web/testing/testing.md","Específico para teste de frontend com Vitest"],"ru":["Требует среды Vitest","Произведено из web/testing/testing.md","Конкретно для тестирования frontend с Vitest"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Vitest","مشتق من web/testing/testing.md","محدد لاختبار واجهة المستخدم مع Vitest"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"f5bcf1878cbd646b6428b07d061545177c8ab2051da65855f1a393478b913568","qualityScore":45}');
